The legal texts come from TanzLII (Judiciary of Tanzania, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  TanzLII, https://tanzlii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as TanzLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting TanzLII as the source (https://tanzlii.org/terms-of-use/).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: TanzLII (https://tanzlii.org), a project of the Judiciary of Tanzania, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws TanzLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither TanzLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

<!-- acts:start -->
Acts of Parliament in acts/<year>/<number>-<short title>/: copies of Acts of the Parliament of the United Republic of
Tanzania as passed, from the Parliament of Tanzania's Acts list (https://polis.bunge.go.tz/), retrieved 2026-11-03 and
2026-11-26. The site states no licence or terms of use. The Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act (Cap. 218),
section 7, gives no protection to laws. The texts are reproduced without change to their wording. Neither the
Parliament of Tanzania nor the Government Printer endorses this repository.

The Constitution in constitution/: the official revised text in English (Cap. 2), published by the Ministry of
Constitutional and Legal Affairs (https://nalis.sheria.go.tz/en/constitution), retrieved 2026-10-28. The site's
footer reads "All Rights Reserved"; the Constitution is law and is not protected (Cap. 218, section 7). Reproduced
without change to its wording; the Ministry does not endorse this repository.

Acts of Parliament not in the Parliament's list, the Revised Laws chapters of the Revised Editions 2019, 2020, 2022
and 2024 not otherwise held (revised-laws/), and subsidiary legislation (subsidiary/): copies from the Office of the
Attorney General's legislation portal, OAG MIS (https://oagmis.oag.go.tz/public), retrieved 2026-11-26. The portal
states no licence or terms of use, and these PDFs carry no reservation. Laws are not protected (Cap. 218, section 7).
The Revised Edition 2023 PDFs, which state "No part of this book may be reproduced or distributed without permission
of OAG", are not included. Reproduced without change to their wording; the Office of the Attorney General does not
endorse this repository.

Secondary copies (commits with a "Source-status: secondary copy (FAOLEX, <URL>)" trailer): Acts and Government
Notices not held from an official host, from FAOLEX, the legislative database of the Food and Agriculture
Organization of the United Nations (https://www.fao.org/faolex/), records listed through ECOLEX
(https://www.ecolex.org), retrieved 2026-11-26. FAO terms: the material may be reproduced for non-commercial
purposes with acknowledgement of FAO as the source (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/en/).
Attribution: Source: FAOLEX Database, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.
The texts are law (Cap. 218, section 7) and are reproduced without change to their wording; FAO does not endorse
this repository.
